ood background in programming or SQL should not take this course. This material complements, but is not required, for the course in machine learning for business applications NBA 6920.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2790, "crseId": 350671, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NBA", "catalogNbr": "6650", "titleShort": "Strat Mgmt of Tech and Innov", "titleLong": "The Strategic Management of Technology and Innovation", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1262, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "10:00AM", "timeEnd": "12:30PM", "startDt": "07/12/2021", "endDt": "07/30/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 4, "netid": "ajf283", "firstName": "Andrew", "middleName": "Joseph", "lastName": "Foley"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3341\nJohnson MBA students are not eligible to enroll."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "07/12/2021", "endDt": "07/30/2021", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPI", "gradingBasisShort": "Opt NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "NBA", "catalogNbr": "2650", "type": "W"}], "sessionCode": "3W3", "sessionBeginDt": "07/12/2021", "sessionEndDt": "07/30/2021", "sessionLong": "Three Week - Three", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This is an introductory management course covering the strategic management of technology and innovation in established firms as well as startup organizations. This course is designed for students who may someday work in, consult for, and/or create firms whose primary product is fundamentally related to technology or innovation. The course typically includes both M.B.A. students and graduate students in science. It starts by examining how industries are transformed by new technologies and how these patterns of industrial change generate both opportunity and high rates of firm failure. We will then explore the questions: Why do some technology leaders fail? and How do technology innovators successfully take on and replace incumbent firms? This leads to an examination of internal management issues, focusing on the design of innovative organizations: designing reward systems, managing growth, overcoming resistance to change, and using organizational culture to promote innovation.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfi